    "body": "fix on issue/3601-gate-build-failure-stops · PR #3708 · pinned by quick_plan_stops_after_a_failed_per_crate_build, metadata_errors_name_the_crate_the_jobs_and_the_package_to_clean, an_ordinary_compile_error_gives_no_metadata_block, a_failed_per_crate_build_stops_the_plan_like_the_whole_gate_build · merges when reviewed\n\nThis PR is a partial fix. It says `Refs #3601`, so this issue stays open.\n\nDone in PR #3708:\n- A failed `<crate> build (--no-run)` step stops the quick plan. The later steps show as \"not run (build failed: <step>)\". The gate exits red.\n- A metadata error (E0786, E0460) prints one `BUILD FAULT` block. The block names the crate and gives two commands: `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4` and `cargo clean -p <package of the step>`. There is no automatic retry or clean.\n\nSeed lead (`xtask/src/seed.rs`), read only:\n- The seed copies registry and git units with the source modification times. It runs one time for each worktree, before the first step, with the cargo locks of the two target directories held.\n- It copies each unit under a temporary name and then renames it. It never copies a local package. It cannot touch the sysroot crate `test`, and one reported error was E0786 for `test`.\n- The seed does not depend on the job count. The failures follow the job count. Thus the seed is not a likely cause.\n- One residual path: the seed replaces a unit that is already in the worktree with a copy of the same hash. A registry crate that does not build reproducibly can then give E0460, on the first gate after a seed only. To exclude it: look for `target/debug/.camcraft-seeded` and the line `target seed: seeded ...` in the failing log, then run again with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`.\n\nRemains open:\n- The cause of the metadata errors at 16 jobs.\n- A reproduction at 16 jobs on the reporting machine.\n- #3675 stays open until a run shows that the stall is gone.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
