    "body": "Codex (m3) read this issue for work on 2026-11-27. I did not claim it. I stopped before a branch, because I cannot reproduce the fault.\n\nWhat I checked on upstream/main 470d1a27c (read only):\n- The quick plan runs each `--no-run` build step alone (`xtask/src/lanes.rs`, `is_build` and `alone`). No other gate step runs at the same time as a build step.\n- One `cargo test -j 16` call builds each dependency one time. Cargo does not start two `rustc` processes for the same unit. The 8 `--test` targets share the dependency units.\n- The unit sweep (`xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs`) runs only at the end of the run. It removes only test-harness units. It cannot touch `png`, `zerocopy`, `accesskit` or the sysroot crate `test`.\n- The seed (`xtask/src/seed.rs`) runs before the first step and does not depend on the job count (see the earlier comment).\n\nResult: I found no path in the gate where two writers change `target\\debug\\deps` at the same time. The errors E0786, E0460 and E0462 on random crates, and on the sysroot crate `test`, point to a file read that sees a partly written or locked file. On Windows, a real-time scanner (Microsoft Defender) or a search indexer can do this. More parallel `rustc` processes make the race more probable. This is a hypothesis. I cannot test it.\n\nWhy I stopped: my host is macOS. The fault shows only on the Windows machine of the reporter. A pinning test that fails on unchanged code is not possible here.\n\nNext step for a person with that machine:\n1. Add the repository `target` directory to the Defender exclusions (Settings > Virus & threat protection > Exclusions).\n2. Run `cargo xtask gate quick --base main` 4 times with the default budget of 16 jobs.\n3. Post the result here. If all 4 runs pass, the cause is the scanner, and the `BUILD FAULT` block can name it as a third thing to try.\n\nPR #3708 already added the `BUILD FAULT` block and the `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4` advice (question 3 of this issue).\n",
